docs/network-design-reference.md:3775:**Dated physical recovery evidence (2026-10-16):** Four disposable equal relays share one public manifest: P/current Mac, R/Windows, Q/mac2015 and S/mac-mini. A bounded precheck establishes that R cannot directly open TCP to S. After preferred P stops, A/current Mac delivers encrypted mail through R→Q→S to B/mac-mini and obtains recipient confirmation. A 130,000-byte consented file survives sender restart before approval, saves matching SHA-256 bytes and returns completion. Stopping Q for at least three seconds leaves the next message absent from B's queried history and A Awaiting; restarting Q with its retained identity restores delivery and confirmation. Disposable profiles/rules are removed; installed services remain untouched.
docs/network-design-reference.md:3777:**Other dated observations:** Disposable clients on the current Mac, Windows and mini completed all 12 directed encrypted DMs through configured legacy/federation paths, and a four-member group exchanged messages across the installed federation. Direct mac2015↔mini and current-Mac↔Windows Tailscale files matched SHA-256. Installed mac2015 and Windows relays separately delivered offline DM/group work to a restarted recipient. SDK pairing across mac2015↔mini preserved original history IDs, sharing off/on behavior and receiver restart persistence.
