### Discovered contacts without chat history

A discovered account that has never had durable sent messages, received messages
or file cards disappears from local contact lists only while offline, once 24
hours have elapsed since its first local roster observation. Current public
presence (including the existing bounded reconnect tolerance) keeps it visible;
any certified ordinary device online protects the account. Returning online
restores even a previously expired contact without resetting its original clock.
Explicit hide/delete controls retain precedence over automatic visibility. The
clock belongs to the local profile and current account;
continuous discovery, name changes, extra devices and application restarts do not
renew it. Existing installations start that clock on their first observation after
upgrade because discovery heartbeat timestamps cannot establish an account's age.
